 "text": "Did you know Helsinki wants AI to heat 70,000 homes? AI actually runs on giant computers in buildings called data centers. Those computers get really hot. To put it into perspective, just one of these computers makes as much heat as 40 kettles boiling non-stop. That's a lot of tea. Normally, data centers just use big fans to blow that heat outside. But Helsinki wants that heat. The city has a plan to use it starting next year. So how would that work? A big new data center would take the heat out of its computers with water in pipes. Then pipes under the streets carry that heat into people's homes. So your chatbot could soon heat an apartment in Helsinki.",
